# WN22-CC-000400: Windows Server 2022 must disable Basic authentication for RSS feeds over HTTP.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-cc-000400-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must disable Basic authentication for RSS feeds over HTTP.`
    description `Basic authentication uses plain-text passwords that could be used to compromise a system. Disabling Basic authentication will reduce this potential.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium,ksi-cmt-rmv,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:CM-7`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `The default behavior is for the Windows RSS platform to not use Basic authentication over HTTP connections. If this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> RSS Feeds >> Turn on Basic feed authentication over HTTP to "Not Configured" or "Disabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_CMT_RMV `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-RMV by setting registry value 'AllowBasicAuthInClear' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Internet Explorer\Feeds' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by setting registry value 'AllowBasicAuthInClear' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Internet Explorer\Feeds' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_CM_7 `Windows Server implements CM-7 by setting registry value 'AllowBasicAuthInClear' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Internet Explorer\Feeds' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Internet Explorer\Feeds`
        name `AllowBasicAuthInClear`
        behavior executor powershell
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 0
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
